      "created": 1792264002553,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Id API_Router        Limit                Window_size         Algorithm\n1   api/v1/search 200tokens/min 120 token(bucket size) Token bucket\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Id API_Router        Limit                Window_size         Algorithm\n1   api/v1/search 200tokens/min 120 token(bucket size) Token bucket\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QUmquPKq73K_Fnmmv63ki",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 468.26659478081604,
      "y": -314.63323160807306,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#da77f2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b11",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2006054284,
      "version": 690,
      "versionNonce": 301295116,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792265276558,
      "created": 1792264151279,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A client sends a request to the Load Balancer, which distributes it across\nmultiple rate limiter instances. Each rate limiter identifies the applicable rule using\nthe API route and user or API key. The rule configuration specifies the rate-\nlimiting algorithm, bucket capacity, and refill rate.\n\nThe rate limiter checks and updates the user's shared rate-limit state in Redis\natomically. For the Token Bucket algorithm, Redis stores the available token\ncount and last-refill timestamp. If a token is available, the rate limiter consumes\none token and forwards the request to the application server. Otherwise, it\nrejects the request with HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests).\n\nA Rule DB stores the persistent rate-limit configuration. A worker can propagate\nconfiguration changes to a cache used by the gateway instances. All rate limiter\ninstances coordinate access to shared rate-limit state so that a user cannot\nbypass the global limit by reaching different instances.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A client sends a request to the Load Balancer, which distributes it across multiple rate limiter instances. Each rate limiter identifies the applicable rule using the API route and user or API key. The rule configuration specifies the rate-limiting algorithm, bucket capacity, and refill rate.\n\nThe rate limiter checks and updates the user's shared rate-limit state in Redis atomically. For the Token Bucket algorithm, Redis stores the available token count and last-refill timestamp. If a token is available, the rate limiter consumes one token and forwards the request to the application server. Otherwise, it rejects the request with HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests).\n\nA Rule DB stores the persistent rate-limit configuration. A worker can propagate configuration changes to a cache used by the gateway instances. All rate limiter instances coordinate access to shared rate-limit state so that a user cannot bypass the global limit by reaching different instances.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
